    content: "### Starting Position\n1. **Stand with feet** shoulder-width apart.\n2. **Position Dumbbells** beside your feet, palms facing your body.\n\n### Grip\n3. **Bend at the hips and knees**, lowering your torso to grasp the dumbbells with both hands.\n\n### Setup\n4. **Keep your back straight** and chest lifted, ensuring your spine is neutral.\n5. **Engage your core** and set your shoulders back.\n\n### Lift\n6. **Drive through your heels**, extending your hips and knees simultaneously.\n7. **Stand up tall**, fully extending your hips and locked knees without leaning back.\n\n### Lowering\n8. **Hinge at the hips** to lower the dumbbells back to the ground, maintaining a flat back.\n9. **Bend your knees** as the weights pass them to return to the starting position.\n\n### Key Points\n- Keep the dumbbells close to your body throughout the movement.\n- Avoid rounding your back; focus on maintaining a neutral spine.\n- Control the movement on the way down to avoid injury.",
